# `use` of an entry file imports its defs and skips its `@target` and drawing lines.
# use_entry.png (128x64): two tiles from `use_entry_part.ramo` and nothing else.
# Left, centered at (40,32): a blue 24x24 square with an ink outline and a gold circle (r 6) at its center.
# Right, centered at (88,32): the same tile with a red square.
# No third tile overlaps the left one at (32,32), where the imported file draws its own tile.
@artboard 128x64
@target targets/use_entry.png

use art/targets/use_entry_part

tile name:a at:40,32
tile name:b at:88,32 tone:p.red
